---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const siteOrigin = (
	Astro.site?.toString() ??
	import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL ??
	'https://jsontosrt.com'
).replace(/\/$/, '');
const canonicalUrl = `${siteOrigin}/terms/`;

const jsonLdGraph = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@graph': [
		{
			'@type': 'Organization',
			'@id': `${siteOrigin}/#organization`,
			name: 'JSON to SRT',
			url: `${siteOrigin}/`,
			email: 'hello@jsontosrt.com',
		},
		{
			'@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
			'@id': `${canonicalUrl}#breadcrumb`,
			itemListElement: [
				{
					'@type': 'ListItem',
					position: 1,
					name: 'JSON to SRT Converter',
					item: `${siteOrigin}/`,
				},
				{
					'@type': 'ListItem',
					position: 2,
					name: 'Terms of Use',
					item: canonicalUrl,
				},
			],
		},
	],
};

const jsonLdSerialized = JSON.stringify(jsonLdGraph).replace(/</g, '\\u003c');
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of Use, MIT License & Disclosure Policy | JSON to SRT"
	description="Read the Terms of Use for jsontosrt.com, including MIT open tool usage, user responsibility to verify final broadcast caption sync, and our rel=sponsored disclosure policy."
	canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
	<article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8">
		<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={jsonLdSerialized} />

		<header class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<div class="inline-flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-slate-100 border border-slate-200 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-slate-800">
				<span>Last Updated: November 12, 2026</span>
				<span class="text-slate-400">/</span>
				<span>MIT Open Tool</span>
			</div>
			<h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-950">
				Terms of Use, MIT Tool License, and Disclosure Policy
			</h1>
			<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
				By accessing or using JSON to SRT (<code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">jsontosrt.com</code>), you agree to these Terms of Use. Because all transcript conversion happens locally inside your web browser, these terms focus on open software licensing, broadcast quality verification responsibilities, and transparent sponsorship disclosures.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">
				1. MIT Open Tool Usage and Your Content Ownership
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
				The client-side JSON parsers, cue reflow algorithms, sample payloads, and interface components of JSON to SRT are original clean-room software provided under the terms of the MIT License. You may use the web converter freely for personal, academic, freelance, studio, or commercial media production with zero file-size caps, watermarks, or registration gates.
			</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
				<li>
					<strong>100% ownership of your transcripts:</strong> We claim zero ownership, license, or rights over any JSON files you load or any <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">.srt</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">.vtt</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">.txt</code>, or <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">.csv</code> files you export. As detailed in our <a href="/privacy/" class="text-sky-700 font-medium hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>, your files never reach our servers.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Authorized input responsibility:</strong> You are solely responsible for ensuring you hold the necessary rights or permission to process the transcripts you load on your local device.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/50 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">
				2. User Responsibility to Verify Final Broadcast Caption Sync and Accuracy
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
				Automated speech recognition models and word-level forced aligners can mishear terminology, drop rapid utterances, misassign overlapping speaker turns, or drift relative to variable-frame-rate (VFR) and drop-frame (29.97 / 59.94 fps) video timelines.
			</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
				<li>
					<strong>Mandatory human QC before broadcast or publication:</strong> You are solely responsible for auditioning and verifying exported subtitle timing synchronization, speaker attribution labels, character reading speed, safe-area line breaks, and spelling inside your non-linear video editor or media player before delivering files to clients, streaming platforms, regulators, or broadcast networks.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Regulatory and accessibility standards:</strong> Automated output from <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-white px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded border border-amber-200">jsontosrt.com</code> does not by itself certify compliance with FCC closed-captioning rules, ADA / Section 508 requirements, WCAG accessibility criteria, EBU-TT, Netflix Timed Text Style Guides, or medical/legal verbatim record standards.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">
				3. Disclaimer of Warranties and Limitation of Liability
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
				Consistent with the MIT License, the website and converter software are provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, and noninfringement. In no event shall the authors or operators of <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">jsontosrt.com</code> be liable for any claim, damages, missed broadcast deadlines, caption rejection fees, or other liability, whether in an action of contract, tort, or otherwise, arising from or in connection with the software or exported subtitle files.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">
				4. Affiliate, Sponsor, and <code class="font-mono text-base">rel="sponsored"</code> Disclosure Policy
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
				Core browser-local JSON-to-subtitle conversion on <a href="/" class="text-sky-700 font-medium hover:underline">jsontosrt.com</a> is free without artificial file-size paywalls. To fund ongoing maintenance and upstream ASR format updates, the site may display clearly labeled developer tool sponsorships, speech-to-text API comparisons, or post-production software affiliate links below or outside the primary converter workbench.
			</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
				<li>
					<strong>Explicit visual disclosure:</strong> Every commercial placement or commission-eligible link includes a plain-language disclosure directly adjacent to the link stating that <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">jsontosrt.com</code> may earn a referral commission or sponsorship fee at no extra cost to you.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>HTML link attribute compliance:</strong> All affiliate and paid sponsor outbound links carry <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">rel="sponsored noopener"</code> in compliance with FTC Endorsement Guides and Google Search link spam policies.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Editorial independence:</strong> Sponsorships never alter parser behavior, never throttle local file sizes, and never gain access to user transcript data.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">
				5. Trademark Non-Affiliation and Contact
			</h2>
			<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
				OpenAI, Whisper, WhisperX, Deepgram, AssemblyAI, Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve, TikTok, and YouTube are trademarks or registered names of their respective owners. JSON to SRT is an independent project; see our <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-700 font-medium hover:underline">About page</a> for technical architecture details. Questions regarding these Terms may be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@jsontosrt.com" class="font-mono font-semibold text-sky-800 underline underline-offset-4 break-words">hello@jsontosrt.com</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
